# m5_graze: the m2_play sweep (without its two holds) plus B held for updates 1600..1619, so
# the bar is spent before the ship meets bullets and a graze can show up in it (a full bar
# would cap the grant). Since M7 it plays in the endless probe mode (debug_probe at 31; a
# normal game dies on this sweep by 1627), and the hold moved from 1960 to 1600 to find a
# clean graze in the M7 waves. 1599: game tick 1569, fuel 180, 6 grazes, 4 probe hits. 1619,
# the last held frame: 20 frames = 40 ticks, game tick 1529, fuel 140; the hold took back the
# graze of 1585 (grazes 5) and the probe hit of 1590 (hits 3). 1620: PLAYING, no tick.
# - 1638 (tick 1547): the ship re-lives that graze: grazes 5 -> 6, but it is under the graze
#   high-water mark, so it pays nothing (fuel 142 before and after).
# - 1714 (tick 1623): a new graze: grazes 6 -> 7 and fuel 150 -> 152. Refill alone cannot
#   get there: 94 live ticks since the release (1529 -> 1623) give at most 140 + (9 + 94) / 10
#   = 150 (9 = the most the refill counter can carry in), and the fuel is 152.
# No rewind is spent (probe mode never rewinds; rewinds stay 3).
--frames 2200 --call-at "31 debug_probe" --dump-exports debug_state,debug_rewinds,debug_fuel,debug_grazes --at "1599 debug_state == 1" --at "1599 debug_game_tick == 1569" --at "1599 debug_fuel == 180" --at "1599 debug_grazes == 6" --at "1599 debug_hits == 4" --at "1600 debug_state == 5" --at "1619 debug_game_tick == 1529" --at "1619 debug_fuel == 140" --at "1619 debug_grazes == 5" --at "1619 debug_hits == 3" --at "1620 debug_state == 1" --at "1630 debug_history_check == 0" --at "1637 debug_grazes == 5" --at "1637 debug_fuel == 142" --at "1638 debug_grazes == 6" --at "1638 debug_fuel == 142" --at "1713 debug_grazes == 6" --at "1713 debug_fuel == 150" --at "1714 debug_game_tick == 1623" --at "1714 debug_grazes == 7" --at "1714 debug_fuel == 152" --at "1714 debug_history_check == 0" --expect "debug_state == 1" --expect "debug_rewinds == 3" --expect "debug_grazes >= 7"
